WEBVTT

00:12.700 --> 00:13.570
Kumi!

00:25.080 --> 00:27.710
You've gotten much better, Aya!

00:27.710 --> 00:29.670
Thank you very much.

00:29.670 --> 00:33.420
If you don't get it together, Kumi, your starting center position might get taken away.

00:33.420 --> 00:34.840
Y-Yeah.

00:35.180 --> 00:40.140
We'll defeat Keishin again this time, for sure...

00:40.140 --> 00:42.730
Yep, yep. I'm looking forward to that.

00:43.430 --> 00:47.730
This upcoming match with Keishin will really motivate us.

00:47.730 --> 00:49.230
That's right!

00:49.230 --> 00:50.480
Let's do our best.

00:50.480 --> 00:52.610
I'll do my best, too.

00:53.400 --> 00:55.990
You all sound so weak.

00:58.950 --> 00:59.990
Rena!

00:59.990 --> 01:01.240
Why are <i>you</i> here?

01:01.580 --> 01:04.660
I was thinking maybe I should start playing basketball again.

01:04.660 --> 01:06.500
So I'm back.

01:06.500 --> 01:09.880
We don't have a spot for you, even if you <i>are </i>back.

01:12.130 --> 01:16.510
Do you understand how much the others have put into their practice in your place?

01:17.010 --> 01:19.510
Those who are not serious will drag the team down.

01:22.220 --> 01:24.140
Please wait, Sensei.

01:25.180 --> 01:28.020
I know I have no right to say anything here,

01:28.020 --> 01:29.770
but please let Rena come back.

01:31.900 --> 01:33.280
Miyu...

01:38.400 --> 01:41.490
Make them see that halation!

01:41.490 --> 01:44.910
We'll carry out the oath we made that day.

01:44.910 --> 01:47.990
Spread out, new formation!

01:47.990 --> 01:51.460
We can see the signs as we call out for one another.

01:51.460 --> 01:57.750
Place your hopes in it, shoot, and watch the arch!

01:58.040 --> 02:02.670
I believe in you, do it like you always do.

02:02.670 --> 02:04.340
Leave it to me.

02:04.340 --> 02:10.890
Put your hands on your chest, and calm yourself down.

02:10.890 --> 02:17.190
I remember each and every granted wish,

02:17.190 --> 02:23.070
including that day I cried in secret.

02:23.070 --> 02:26.570
We're not the only ones

02:26.570 --> 02:30.120
seeing these same dreams.

02:30.120 --> 02:33.750
The sparks in those unyielding eyes

02:33.750 --> 02:36.880
that appeared in front of me,

02:36.880 --> 02:38.460
let them fly!

02:38.750 --> 02:41.880
Make them see that halation!

02:41.880 --> 02:45.220
Run into that open space!

02:45.220 --> 02:51.850
This lingering sensation, looking back on those carefree days.

02:51.850 --> 02:58.400
After saying farewell, you smile with everyone else,

02:58.400 --> 03:04.690
aim for the place you dreamed of, shoot, and watch the arch!

03:11.790 --> 03:12.290
Tomo!

03:12.290 --> 03:13.290
Got it!

03:15.670 --> 03:18.090
One more week until the tournament, huh?

03:18.510 --> 03:21.180
I think everyone has gotten much better, but...

03:21.180 --> 03:25.430
We've done all we can this last month.

03:25.430 --> 03:28.060
But we're up against Suzuridani.

03:28.060 --> 03:31.560
And also, Natsuhi-kun told me about a player they have named Rena-san.

03:33.100 --> 03:38.070
Ashihara Rena never used the same drive twice against my sisters.

03:38.400 --> 03:42.530
So that means she's mastered plenty of skill moves?

03:42.530 --> 03:43.660
Yeah.

03:43.660 --> 03:47.910
I only saw her once, so I don't know if I can do them exactly like her.

03:48.370 --> 03:49.830
That's fine.

03:49.830 --> 03:53.420
Just show me what you remember.

03:54.380 --> 03:55.460
All right.

03:56.090 --> 03:57.300
Here I go.

04:01.340 --> 04:07.890
That move Natsuhi-kun did isn't something a normal elementary schooler can do.

04:07.890 --> 04:11.230
If Rena-san can really use that...

04:11.560 --> 04:16.060
I'll teach Tsubaki-chan and
Hiiragi-chan how to guard her.

04:16.060 --> 04:18.650
The rest is up to their own strength.

04:18.650 --> 04:19.980
One more time!

04:20.320 --> 04:21.860
Here, Tsuba! Pass!

04:22.070 --> 04:23.450
Okay!

04:23.450 --> 04:24.530
Got it!

04:24.780 --> 04:27.200
Hey! What are you doing, Hii?

04:27.200 --> 04:29.330
Your pass was no good!

04:29.330 --> 04:33.040
Hey, you can't blame each other, you know?

04:33.040 --> 04:36.380
What are you saying, Maho? If you go easy on us, then we won't win!

04:36.380 --> 04:37.500
That's right!

04:37.500 --> 04:39.090
Okay! Tsuba, one more time!

04:39.090 --> 04:41.090
All right! You too, Maho!

04:41.090 --> 04:44.050
Jeez, what's with you two?

04:46.800 --> 04:49.720
We'll definitely defeat Rena and beat Suzuridani!

04:49.720 --> 04:51.100
Yeah, that's right!

04:51.220 --> 04:54.640
We need to practice our butts off even more!

04:54.640 --> 04:55.350
Yeah!

04:57.650 --> 05:00.610
That's right. There's no point to all this if we don't win.

05:00.860 --> 05:03.440
Hey! You've been missing your shots, Masami.

05:03.440 --> 05:05.320
You're slacking off too much!

05:05.490 --> 05:07.820
Huh? What are you two saying?

05:07.820 --> 05:10.870
I've been practicing a lot more than the two of you!

05:10.870 --> 05:13.080
H-Hey, stop it, you guys.

05:13.080 --> 05:15.210
Everyone has bad days.

05:15.210 --> 05:16.120
Yes, yes.

05:16.120 --> 05:18.750
Gettan, you too! Your movements are too stiff!

05:18.750 --> 05:20.800
Huh? R-Really?

05:20.800 --> 05:22.090
Pull it together!

05:22.090 --> 05:24.420
And Mimi, pass the ball more!

05:24.420 --> 05:26.800
I look at the situation, then pass.

05:26.800 --> 05:29.640
To put it simply, we can't afford to mess up!

05:29.640 --> 05:31.470
We have to practice a lot more!

05:32.560 --> 05:34.890
There now.

05:34.890 --> 05:38.230
If you're that strict on yourself, you'll burn out.

05:39.520 --> 05:40.730
She's right.

05:40.730 --> 05:44.320
There are things more important than conditioning for a match.

05:44.320 --> 05:47.610
Oh! Resting is important, too.

05:47.610 --> 05:49.870
You have to eat a lot, too.

05:49.870 --> 05:53.660
Everyone, just relax, okay?

05:58.710 --> 06:03.000
They all said that stuff, but we can't win without practicing.

06:03.000 --> 06:05.050
Our regimen right now is too weak.

06:05.050 --> 06:07.840
Yes, that's right. It should be tougher.

06:07.840 --> 06:10.140
Otherwise there's no point in all of us practicing together.

06:10.140 --> 06:12.810
I agree with you on that.

06:12.810 --> 06:15.810
We only have one more week left. We've got to practice even more.

06:16.060 --> 06:18.690
Okay! We'll tell the coach directly tomorrow!

06:19.020 --> 06:20.560
Yeah!

06:23.150 --> 06:27.400
We only have one more week left... that's not much time.

06:27.400 --> 06:28.450
Oh?

06:28.450 --> 06:30.200
What's the matter, Kage?

06:31.280 --> 06:34.330
I'm sorry for worrying you, Nee-sama.

06:34.330 --> 06:39.080
I just feel so nervous thinking that we only have a week left until the game.

06:39.080 --> 06:40.460
Oh!

06:40.460 --> 06:43.340
Relax. You'll be just fine, Kage.

06:43.840 --> 06:46.050
I hope that's the case.

06:50.430 --> 06:54.720
<i>Hiiragi, Tsubaki, and Masami are all too vested in winning.</i>

06:54.720 --> 06:58.350
<i>And Kagetsu is too stiff
because of her nervousness.</i>

07:01.650 --> 07:04.570
<i>Looks like it's all up to me now!</i>

07:05.480 --> 07:09.360
How's practice going? Are the fifth-years listening to you?

07:11.280 --> 07:14.160
For now, I guess.

07:14.160 --> 07:17.580
I've already told the
sixth-years about their positions.

07:17.580 --> 07:19.790
I think we'll be fine.

07:20.210 --> 07:22.290
If that's what you say.

07:22.670 --> 07:25.290
I actually have high expectations for you, Coach.

07:25.290 --> 07:27.960
Ouch! You patted me too hard!

07:28.920 --> 07:32.720
This is the first and last
tournament for the sixth-years.

07:34.510 --> 07:35.810
Yeah.

07:36.810 --> 07:37.680
Hmm...

07:37.680 --> 07:40.350
Teaching other people is really hard!

07:40.350 --> 07:41.390
Yeah.

07:41.390 --> 07:43.940
You have to explain things in a way that they can understand.

07:43.940 --> 07:45.400
It's super hard.

07:45.400 --> 07:47.900
Being a coach must be really tough.

07:47.900 --> 07:49.030
Oh!

07:49.030 --> 07:52.570
Onii-chan has been teaching us all this time! He's amazing!

07:52.570 --> 07:53.780
That's right.

07:53.780 --> 07:56.280
Subaru-san has been our coach this entire time.

07:56.280 --> 07:57.830
He protects us all...

07:57.830 --> 07:59.620
I'm really grateful for that.

07:59.620 --> 08:01.000
Oh, that's right!

08:01.000 --> 08:03.460
Tomo, have you decided on when you'll do <i>that</i>?

08:03.460 --> 08:05.750
Huh?! Uh, well...

08:05.750 --> 08:08.670
I think I'll do it after the game.

08:08.670 --> 08:11.510
You better tell him how we feel, too.

08:11.510 --> 08:12.630
O-Okay!

08:12.630 --> 08:14.010
I'll do my best!

08:32.860 --> 08:36.200
I see you still just can't take even a single day off.

08:36.200 --> 08:37.870
It's so cold today, too.

08:39.160 --> 08:41.580
It's because this is all I have.

08:41.910 --> 08:45.330
I really want to let Rena to hear that.

08:45.330 --> 08:50.500
You persuaded the coach to include Rena on the bench, right?

08:50.500 --> 08:52.090
Thank you very much.

08:52.380 --> 08:55.590
Well, everyone knows about her talent.

08:57.720 --> 09:02.480
Maybe you're seeing the old you in her?

09:04.980 --> 09:07.730
Think whatever you would like.

09:13.030 --> 09:15.240
Coach! We have a request!

09:16.490 --> 09:18.740
Please be tougher on us!

09:18.740 --> 09:22.700
Yes! We can't beat Rena or Suzuridani like this!

09:22.700 --> 09:27.500
We don't have much time left! Please let us practice more!

09:27.500 --> 09:30.500
Everyone! Tell the coach you want to practice more, too!

09:30.500 --> 09:32.760
Yeah! You're all not pumped up enough!

09:32.760 --> 09:34.130
Please!

09:39.600 --> 09:42.770
Let's play a mini-game first.

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Name

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Aida Miyu

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Date of birth

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Blood type

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Class

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Suzuridani Girls School
6th Year, Class 1

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Height

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Bust size

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
A bit tiny for a sixth-year...

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Person she respects

09:47.020 --> 09:50.020
Allen Iverson

09:55.030 --> 09:57.910
<i>Subaru-san, what are you trying to do?</i>

10:02.700 --> 10:04.660
Let's start then.

10:06.910 --> 10:07.870
Here I go, Tsuba!

10:07.870 --> 10:08.790
Yeah!

10:09.790 --> 10:10.670
What?!

10:11.710 --> 10:12.340
Maho!

10:12.340 --> 10:13.380
Got it!

10:13.380 --> 10:13.960
Mokkan!

10:14.210 --> 10:15.090
Airi!

10:17.760 --> 10:18.720
Maho-chan!

10:29.520 --> 10:31.520
Hey, what are you doing?!

10:33.440 --> 10:37.570
<i>I see... I know what Subaru-san is trying to tell them.</i>

10:38.700 --> 10:41.070
Hey, Subaru, don't tell me...

10:47.250 --> 10:47.960
Okay.

10:56.420 --> 10:57.050
Saki!

11:04.220 --> 11:05.060
No!

11:05.060 --> 11:05.720
Airi!

11:05.720 --> 11:06.560
Okay!

11:18.650 --> 11:19.110
Oh!

11:19.110 --> 11:20.150
No!

11:22.820 --> 11:24.580
6th Years

11:22.820 --> 11:24.580
5th Years

11:25.450 --> 11:28.080
Our shots aren't going in at all.

11:28.500 --> 11:31.080
We can't stop them.

11:31.080 --> 11:33.080
I can't figure out their fakes.

11:33.080 --> 11:35.710
We really <i>do</i> have to practice even more!

11:35.710 --> 11:37.760
Yeah! We can't beat Rena like this!

11:38.380 --> 11:41.380
That's right... We have to work even harder...

11:41.380 --> 11:43.510
That's wrong.

11:46.310 --> 11:48.470
What are you talking about?

11:48.720 --> 11:51.230
We lost because we didn't practice enough, right?

11:51.230 --> 11:53.350
What other reason is there?

11:53.520 --> 11:55.230
Tomo is right.

11:55.230 --> 11:57.940
You're all full of openings because you're so stiff.

11:57.940 --> 12:00.610
Normally you'd be able to score more off of us.

12:00.780 --> 12:02.110
Huh?

12:02.280 --> 12:05.570
You might be focusing too much on winning during practice.

12:05.570 --> 12:06.530
Oh!

12:06.530 --> 12:08.620
That's why your emotions are all over the place.

12:08.620 --> 12:12.500
I told you before that practice isn't everything.

12:12.500 --> 12:15.210
There are more important things, you know.

12:15.380 --> 12:18.460
What's more important than winning the game?!

12:18.460 --> 12:21.220
Yeah! We have to beat Rena this time!

12:21.220 --> 12:23.380
She was so mean to Masami!

12:23.380 --> 12:26.010
This might have nothing to do with you, Maho.

12:26.010 --> 12:28.310
But to us, this is personal!

12:28.310 --> 12:30.060
Like hell it has nothing to do with us!

12:31.310 --> 12:33.940
We're on the same team! Of course I'm frustrated!

12:33.940 --> 12:35.560
Isn't that obvious?

12:37.360 --> 12:39.270
I'm sorry, I just...

12:39.270 --> 12:41.740
Of course we want to win the game.

12:41.740 --> 12:46.570
But you're all putting so much effort into it that it's having an adverse effect.

12:46.950 --> 12:49.450
You can't even do things you should be able to.

12:51.910 --> 12:55.080
There was a time when I was like that, too.

12:55.080 --> 12:56.330
Huh?

12:57.080 --> 13:00.300
Before I transferred here and met all of you,

13:00.300 --> 13:04.590
I kept thinking that I had to help the team win and practiced by myself.

13:05.680 --> 13:08.720
But now, everyone is with me.

13:08.720 --> 13:12.680
They're helping me protect the game I love so much.

13:13.770 --> 13:19.190
I feel so comfortable alongside everyone that I can play a lot better now.

13:20.270 --> 13:24.950
I think I'm really fortunate to be able to play basketball right now.

13:28.160 --> 13:31.290
Suzuridani is a really strong team.

13:31.290 --> 13:35.710
But if you think too hard about it, you may let victory fall from your grasp.

13:35.710 --> 13:40.710
It's hard to explain, but the more nervous you are, the more you need to relax, right?

13:40.710 --> 13:45.800
And we're finally all friends now. We need to enjoy ourselves.

13:45.800 --> 13:50.720
Oh! Do you not like playing basketball with all of us, Tsuba, Hii?

13:51.390 --> 13:53.020
Well...

13:53.020 --> 13:54.480
I mean...

13:55.140 --> 13:59.270
Nee-sama and the others have never been in an official tournament, right?

13:59.270 --> 14:02.110
They have faced much more
disappointment than we have.

14:03.690 --> 14:05.780
Please play us again.

14:06.860 --> 14:09.110
We'll do it properly this time.

14:12.490 --> 14:14.750
Okay! One more time, then!

14:14.750 --> 14:16.500
That's right. Let's do it.

14:16.500 --> 14:18.000
Oh! Roger!

14:18.000 --> 14:19.830
Yep, let's do our best!

14:22.800 --> 14:25.010
Mokkan! You're so slow!

14:25.010 --> 14:27.090
Sorry! Let's go!

14:30.930 --> 14:34.770
I wonder if the girls realize how much they've grown.

14:35.020 --> 14:40.270
Yeah, I'm really happy that they can all think and learn by themselves.

14:40.270 --> 14:42.770
So you say, but aren't you actually a bit lonely?

14:44.190 --> 14:45.820
Well, maybe a little.

14:45.820 --> 14:50.530
The more they mature, the less we can do.

14:52.370 --> 14:53.780
You're right.

14:56.500 --> 14:58.410
Thanks, Subaru.

14:58.710 --> 15:00.120
For what?

15:00.120 --> 15:02.250
For inviting me to become a coach.

15:02.250 --> 15:04.420
I didn't think it'd be this fun.

15:05.340 --> 15:08.420
I'm sure that on the day of the match, it'll be even more fun.

15:08.720 --> 15:11.180
Yep, you're right.

15:58.640 --> 16:01.640
The 44th Region 2 Girls' Mini-Basketball Qualifying Tournament

16:01.140 --> 16:04.400
Keishin Academy

16:01.140 --> 16:04.400
Suzuridani Girls School

16:09.780 --> 16:14.030
As a team, and as friends, let's do our best!

16:14.030 --> 16:15.120
Okay!

16:15.780 --> 16:21.540
There are three phrases you must never forget in mini-basketball.

16:21.790 --> 16:22.830
Oh?

16:22.830 --> 16:24.040
Phrases?

16:24.830 --> 16:27.790
Friendship, smiles, and fair play.

16:28.920 --> 16:30.960
That's exactly how we play!

16:30.960 --> 16:35.140
Yeah, that's your very own style of basketball.

16:35.140 --> 16:35.970
That's why...

16:35.970 --> 16:37.640
We won't forget today!

16:37.640 --> 16:39.720
We'll fight as a team!

16:39.970 --> 16:41.230
Yes.

16:41.480 --> 16:44.480
Okay. Enjoy the game to its fullest!

16:45.020 --> 16:47.560
Keishin Girls' Basketball Team!

16:47.560 --> 16:48.730
Fight!

16:48.730 --> 16:51.240
Yeah!

16:54.150 --> 16:56.240
This won't end like last time.

16:56.780 --> 16:58.490
We'll do our best!

17:05.120 --> 17:05.750
Maho-chan!

17:06.040 --> 17:06.920
Got it!

17:06.920 --> 17:07.420
Saki!

17:14.300 --> 17:17.260
You're putting the sixth-years as your starting rotation?

17:17.260 --> 17:20.430
There's a rule saying you have to put all your players in at some point, right?

17:20.430 --> 17:21.680
Yeah.

17:21.680 --> 17:24.230
I'll put in the fifth-years when the second quarter starts.

17:24.230 --> 17:26.520
I'm sure Suzuridani has the same plan.

17:26.520 --> 17:29.110
The kids must have figured it out, too.

17:33.900 --> 17:37.490
We're both trying to gauge each other.

17:37.490 --> 17:39.490
I want to run up the score, if we can.

17:39.490 --> 17:40.490
Yeah.

17:45.330 --> 17:46.120
<i>This girl...</i>

17:46.830 --> 17:48.750
<i>Make them come close to you...</i>

17:52.590 --> 17:53.510
<i>Now!</i>

17:59.180 --> 18:02.140
Oh! Nice shot, Airi!

18:02.140 --> 18:03.810
We got the first basket!

18:03.810 --> 18:05.680
Keishin Academy

18:03.810 --> 18:05.680
Suzuridani Girls School

18:06.520 --> 18:11.650
That center is a lot different from last time, both in power and mental strength!

18:12.520 --> 18:14.190
I'll watch her closely.

18:17.530 --> 18:19.030
<i>I have to stop her.</i>

18:21.330 --> 18:22.490
Oh!

18:23.990 --> 18:25.000
<i>So fast!</i>

18:27.040 --> 18:27.830
Oh!

18:32.960 --> 18:34.210
Oh!

18:39.470 --> 18:41.220
Keishin Academy

18:39.470 --> 18:41.220
Suzuridani Girls School

18:41.600 --> 18:42.760
Amazing...

18:42.760 --> 18:45.220
They're taking the lead against Suzuridani!

18:45.890 --> 18:48.690
Keishin has risen to another level.

18:48.690 --> 18:49.730
Yeah.

18:51.730 --> 18:52.230
Tomo!

18:54.020 --> 18:54.650
Maho!

18:54.650 --> 18:55.230
Got it!

18:56.440 --> 18:56.900
Hina!

18:57.570 --> 18:58.240
Oh!

18:59.530 --> 19:00.410
No!

19:06.450 --> 19:11.210
Keishin Academy

19:06.450 --> 19:11.210
Suzuridani Girls School

19:09.500 --> 19:11.210
You girls suck!

19:11.500 --> 19:13.540
You're losing already.

19:13.540 --> 19:15.550
Against such a weak team, too.

19:15.550 --> 19:16.960
R-Rena...

19:17.260 --> 19:20.090
You'd better watch your words, or they'll come back to bite you.

19:21.340 --> 19:26.850
That center and small forward have both gotten much better since last time.

19:26.850 --> 19:29.730
Keishin's skill has risen quite a bit.

19:30.520 --> 19:33.480
We'll study Keishin's players during the second quarter,

19:33.480 --> 19:36.190
and come up with a counter for the third.

19:36.190 --> 19:38.400
I'm sure you can tie it back up!

19:38.400 --> 19:39.490
Do your best!

19:39.650 --> 19:40.820
Okay!

19:40.820 --> 19:44.370
You don't need to work that hard. I can win all by myself.

19:45.990 --> 19:47.370
Good job, everyone!

19:47.370 --> 19:49.290
It's amazing how you've taken the lead!

19:49.290 --> 19:50.620
Nice rhythm, too!

19:51.120 --> 19:53.040
How did it feel?

19:53.040 --> 19:54.080
They're strong!

19:54.080 --> 19:56.210
They scored right back at us!

19:56.210 --> 19:57.050
Oh!

19:57.050 --> 19:58.960
They all move so fast!

19:58.960 --> 20:01.510
That tiny girl with the ribbon is really good!

20:01.510 --> 20:04.970
I feel like they're still measuring us out.

20:04.970 --> 20:07.390
I think they're holding back quite a bit.

20:07.640 --> 20:11.770
Just keep this up into the third quarter.

20:11.770 --> 20:13.400
It's your turn now, fifth-years.

20:13.400 --> 20:15.730
It's gonna be a piece of cake, leave it to us.

20:15.730 --> 20:18.070
We'll run up the score even more!

20:18.070 --> 20:20.990
Ashihara Rena is in, too. We can't lose!

20:20.990 --> 20:22.070
We'll do our best!

20:22.070 --> 20:24.320
We'll enjoy the game to its fullest!

20:25.620 --> 20:26.870
Do your best!

20:26.870 --> 20:28.330
That's what I'm planning to do.

20:28.540 --> 20:29.700
Fight!

20:29.700 --> 20:31.830
I'll use what you've taught me, Master.

20:32.040 --> 20:33.920
Don't go easy on them.

20:33.920 --> 20:35.380
Of course!

20:35.540 --> 20:38.630
I'm looking forward to the dynamic twin duo!

20:38.630 --> 20:39.840
You won't be disappointed!

20:40.050 --> 20:42.550
The center supports everyone!

20:42.550 --> 20:43.630
Yes!

20:43.630 --> 20:45.590
Keishin Academy

20:43.630 --> 20:45.590
Suzuridani Girls School

20:47.050 --> 20:50.640
Well then, come at me if you want to feel despair.

20:53.390 --> 20:55.190
I'll go.

20:55.190 --> 20:56.190
Masami!

20:58.360 --> 21:01.320
I'm here to hear your apology regarding what happened at the Gourmet Fair.

21:01.320 --> 21:05.780
I told you that wasn't my fault.

21:05.780 --> 21:08.990
Well, I won't lose so I don't have to apologize.

21:10.200 --> 21:12.950
Come on now. Here I go!

21:12.950 --> 21:14.580
Is she gonna use it?

21:17.960 --> 21:19.840
You won't steal anything like that!

21:23.010 --> 21:25.970
Let me start with the disappearing ball!

21:39.860 --> 21:41.480
Do you understand now?

21:41.480 --> 21:44.070
I'm on a completely different level.

21:45.400 --> 21:47.660
So it seems.

21:55.580 --> 21:58.330
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

21:58.330 --> 21:59.870
Rolling! Rolling!

21:59.870 --> 22:02.790
Keep on bouncing!

22:01.080 --> 22:03.800
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

22:03.800 --> 22:06.210
Elementary schoolers are the best!

22:06.210 --> 22:06.590
Yay!

22:10.680 --> 22:15.680
Our bodies and our hearts are size SS,

22:16.180 --> 22:21.600
but our dreams can be size LL, can't they? Can't they?

22:21.600 --> 22:26.990
Adolescents have lots of troubles,

22:26.990 --> 22:32.570
but we'll overcome them together.

22:32.570 --> 22:38.000
I want to get even better!

22:33.370 --> 22:34.740
Even

22:34.740 --> 22:36.080
better!

22:38.000 --> 22:45.670
I want to see your face when I surprise you!

22:38.960 --> 22:39.620
Ooh!

22:40.290 --> 22:41.000
Wow!

22:45.880 --> 22:48.590
Just keep on spinning!

22:48.590 --> 22:52.510
The Earth is one big basketball!

22:52.510 --> 22:56.180
I'll believe in the future and move forward!

22:55.560 --> 22:56.870
I'll keep going!

22:56.810 --> 22:59.520
Just keep on spinning!

22:59.520 --> 23:03.480
The universe is one big basketball court!

23:03.480 --> 23:06.900
I want you to receive it.

23:06.190 --> 23:07.150
Ready, and!

23:06.900 --> 23:08.740
Pass! Pass! Pass!

23:09.150 --> 23:11.150
Please take it!

23:12.410 --> 23:15.160
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

23:15.160 --> 23:16.700
Rolling! Rolling!

23:16.700 --> 23:19.580
Keep on bouncing!

23:17.830 --> 23:20.580
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

23:20.580 --> 23:23.040
Elementary schoolers are the best!

23:23.040 --> 23:24.980
Yay!

23:25.210 --> 23:26.420
Isn't it getting a bit crowded here?

23:26.420 --> 23:27.630
Don't say that!

23:27.630 --> 23:28.590
We're running out of time!

23:28.590 --> 23:29.380
We've got to hurry!

23:29.380 --> 23:31.220
Oh! A word from everybody!

23:31.220 --> 23:32.050
Okay!

23:32.050 --> 23:32.640
Hey!

23:32.640 --> 23:33.680
Just a little bit.

23:33.680 --> 23:34.890
That's so old.

23:34.890 --> 23:35.970
Mimi, how do you know that?

23:35.970 --> 23:38.100
In any case, let's all do our best!

23:36.950 --> 23:40.000
Next episode

23:38.100 --> 23:39.890
Yeah!
